---
id: org.dxos.plugin.higgsfield
name: HiggsfieldPlugin
version: 0.1.0
---

A **headless** Composer plugin that makes [Higgsfield](https://higgsfield.ai) available as an
**image** and **video** generation provider for `plugin-studio`. No React/UI surfaces.

## Extensions

| Term   | URI                     |
| ------ | ----------------------- |
| `feat` | `org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0` |
| `test` | `org.dxos.mdl.test@1.0` |

## Connector

```mdl
feat HiggsfieldConnector
  desc: >
    Contributes a ConnectorEntry via Capability.contribute(Connector, [entry]) on
    ConnectorEvents.Start (mirrors plugin-heygen / plugin-ideogram).
  id: org.dxos.plugin.higgsfield.connector
  source: higgsfield.ai
  label: Higgsfield
  credentialForm:
    schema: HiggsfieldCredentialForm { keyId: string, keySecret: string (password) }
    onSubmit: >
      Trim both parts and require both; store Obj.make(AccessToken, { source: "higgsfield.ai",
      token: "<keyId>:<keySecret>" }) + Obj.make(Connection, { connectorId, accessToken });
      return { kind: "complete", … }.
```

## Provider

```mdl
feat HiggsfieldGenerationService
  desc: >
    Contributes two GenerationServices (kinds 'image' and 'video', one shared HiggsfieldProvider)
    via Capability.contributeAll(StudioCapabilities.GenerationService, services) on
    StudioEvents.Start. Asynchronous: enqueue → awaitResult (poll). Contract from
    @dxos/plugin-studio/GenerationService.
  id: higgsfield
  kinds: [image, video]
  contentType: image/jpeg | video/mp4          # per service; the produced media decides the variant mime
  source: higgsfield.ai
  requestSchema:
    image: { model, prompt }
    video: { model, prompt, imageUrl?, stillModel? }   # DoP animates a still: generated from the prompt unless imageUrl is given
  fieldOptions:
    image.model: Soul v2 / Soul (text-to-image)
    video.model: DoP lite / turbo / standard (image-to-video); video.stillModel: the Soul tiers
  defaultRequest:
    image: { model: "higgsfield-ai/soul/v2/standard" }
    video: { model: "higgsfield-ai/dop/lite", stillModel: "higgsfield-ai/soul/v2/standard" }
  enqueue:
    endpoint: POST https://api.higgsfield.ai/<model>   # via edge CORS proxy; header Authorization: Key id:secret
    body: { prompt } (image) | { prompt, image_url } (video — the still is a synchronous Soul job inside enqueue)
    returns: { jobId: request_id }   # the animation's id for video
  awaitResult:
    endpoint: GET https://api.higgsfield.ai/requests/{jobId}/status   # 2s → 10s backoff, 5 min timeout
    terminal: completed | failed | nsfw | canceled
    returns: variants from images[].url (image/jpeg) | video.url (video/mp4) | audio(s) (audio/mpeg)
    progress: onProgress({ status: Queued | Generating | … })
  errors:
    - missing credential → MissingCredential (studio resolves it from the Connector credential first)
    - blank model path → ProviderFailure
    - non-2xx submit / 4xx status / failed / nsfw / canceled / timeout → ProviderFailure
    - 5xx on status → retried
```

## Dependencies

- `@dxos/plugin-studio` (workspace:\*) — `GenerationService` contract, `StudioCapabilities`, `StudioEvents`.
- `@dxos/plugin-connector`, `@dxos/link` (AccessToken/Connection), `@dxos/edge-client` (CORS proxy),
  `@dxos/app-framework`, `@dxos/echo`, `@dxos/log`, `@dxos/util`, `effect`.

## Out of scope (v1)

- Image-to-video / reference-media inputs (file upload flow).
- Model picker (no public catalog endpoint), cancellation, webhooks.

## QA

Executable tests. Each step carries a human instruction (`do`) and, where the step maps to an
invocable operation, an agent binding (`invoke`). Report failures by test and step number.

```mdl
test QA-1: Connect Higgsfield and generate an image
  desc: |
    Higgsfield is headless — it contributes a Connector credential form and GenerationServices,
    but owns no UI and no operation of its own. Generation runs entirely through plugin-studio's
    generic `Generate` operation with `provider: "higgsfield"`.
  actors: both
  covers: [HiggsfieldConnector, HiggsfieldGenerationService]
  status: unverified
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - space: a space is open
    - collection: a collection in that space, to create into
    - a Higgsfield Cloud API key id + secret on an account with credits
    - no Artifact named "QA Soul Image" exists — ABORT rather than reusing one this test did not create
  steps:
    - name: Connect Higgsfield
      do: Open Settings -> Connectors -> Higgsfield, enter the API key ID and secret, and submit.
      expect: a Connection + AccessToken pair for source "higgsfield.ai" now exists, token "<id>:<secret>"
      note: |
        NO `invoke` — credential submission goes through the Connector's `onSubmit` UI callback,
        not an operation with a runtime key.
    - name: Create an image Artifact
      do: In the navtree, click + on a collection and choose Studio Artifact, kind Image. Name it "QA Soul Image".
      capture: created
      expect: an Artifact of kind "image" named "QA Soul Image" exists
      note: |
        NO `invoke` — `Artifact.make()` is wired through `CreateObjectEntry`; there is no operation
        key behind object creation itself.
    - name: Generate with Higgsfield
      do: In the Artifact's generate panel, pick "Higgsfield" as the provider, leave the model at its default, enter a prompt, and click Generate.
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.studio.generate { artifact: $created.object, provider: "higgsfield", config: { model: "higgsfield-ai/soul/v2/standard", prompt: "A quiet alpine lake at sunrise" } }
      capture: generated
      expect: |
        the invoke blocks until the request reaches a terminal state (enqueue + awaitResult both
        run inside the operation), and the filled Variant holds an image/jpeg URL
      assert: |
        const artifact = await space.db.load($created.object);
        const last = await space.db.load(artifact.variants[artifact.variants.length - 1]);
        return $generated.count >= 1 && last.contentType === 'image/jpeg' && typeof last.url === 'string' && last.url.startsWith('https://');
      note: Async provider — `enqueue` returns the request_id, `awaitResult` polls `GET /requests/{id}/status` until 'completed' before the operation returns.
  after:
    - name: Delete the Artifact
      do: Right-click "QA Soul Image" in the navtree and choose Delete.
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.space.removeObjects { objects: [$created.object], target: $given.collection }
      expect: the row leaves the navtree and its plank closes if it was open
    - name: Disconnect Higgsfield
      do: In Settings -> Connectors -> Higgsfield, remove the connection.
      expect: the Connection and its AccessToken are removed
```
